            "annotations": [],
            "text": "# Netflix (NFLX) vs. Disney (DIS): 3-Year Revenue Growth & Operating Margin\n\nBoth companies just closed FY2025 (Netflix: Dec 2025; Disney: Sep 2025), so the \"last three fiscal years\" covers FY2023 \u2192 FY2025, with FY2022 shown as the prior-year base for growth calculations.\n\n## Revenue\n\n| Fiscal Year | NFLX Revenue | NFLX YoY | DIS Revenue | DIS YoY |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| FY2022 (base) | $31.62B | \u2014 | $82.72B | \u2014 |\n| FY2023 | $33.72B | +6.7% | $88.90B | +7.5% |\n| FY2024 | $39.00B | +15.7% | $91.36B | +2.8% |\n| FY2025 | $45.18B | +15.9% | $94.43B | +3.4% |\n\n**3-year revenue CAGR (FY22 \u2192 FY25):** NFLX **+12.7%** vs. DIS **+4.5%**.\n\n## Operating Margin\n\n| Fiscal Year | NFLX Op. Margin | NFLX Op. Profit | DIS Op. Margin | DIS Op. Profit |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| FY2023 | 21% | $6.95B | 6% | $5.10B |\n| FY2024 | 27% | $10.42B | 9% | $8.32B |\n| FY2025 | 29% | $13.33B | 14% | $13.01B |\n\n**Margin expansion (FY23 \u2192 FY25):** NFLX **+8 pts** (21% \u2192 29%); DIS **+8 pts** (6% \u2192 14%).\n\n## Takeaways\n\n- **Growth:** Netflix's top line is compounding roughly **3\u00d7 faster** than Disney's (12.7% vs. 4.5% CAGR). Netflix accelerated meaningfully in FY2024\u2013FY2025 (mid-teens growth), while Disney's revenue growth has been low single digits since FY2024.\n- **Margins:** Both expanded operating margin by ~8 percentage points, but Netflix now runs at **29%** \u2014 more than double Disney's **14%**. Notably, in FY2025 Netflix generated **more operating profit ($13.33B) than Disney ($13.01B)** on roughly half the revenue.\n- **Trend direction:** Netflix shows a clean, monotonic improvement in both growth and profitability. Disney's margin trajectory reversed a dip (FY2023 fell to 6% from 8% in FY2022) and has since recovered strongly, but revenue growth remains subdued.\n\nBottom line: over the trailing three fiscal years, Netflix has delivered materially better revenue growth and reached a much higher \u2014 and still-widening \u2014 operating-margin structure than Disney, though Disney's margin recovery from the FY2023 trough has been sharp.",
